      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7f353fd_cc83b795",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_spi.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-01T18:19:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "just curious, why there has to be a CMD vs RSP distinction in the ID - isn\u0027t transfer direction self explanatory?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 138,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "e1071ad23f6eb765fdb8ec986989fe1a0ebea442",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41047560_5f53f6ad",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_spi.h",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 138,
      "author": {
        "id": 1347380
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-06-03T09:08:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The packet_id_type values have very similar names in particular on the start and continue packets. I haven\u0027t found a naming scheme that I really think avoids potential confusion unlike some of the others like \u0027GET_USB_SPI_CONFIG\u0027 and \u0027USB_SPI_CONFIG \u0027 which are quite obvious.\n\nI\u0027ve considered naming conventions like \u0027USB_SPI_PKT_ID_WRITE_START\u0027, \u0027USB_SPI_PKT_ID_WRITE_CONTINUE\u0027, \u0027USB_SPI_PKT_ID_READ_START\u0027, \u0027USB_SPI_PKT_ID_READ_CONTINUE\u0027 but I didn\u0027t like that both of the start packets include other information that needs to be transferred.\n\nMaking the direction explicit helps with that concern and gives a quick check that \u0027yes, this is only creating the \u0027RSP\u0027 packets and it is only reading \u0027CMD\u0027 packets.",
      "parentUuid": "b7f353fd_cc83b795",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 138,
        "startChar": 49,
        "endLine": 138,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "e1071ad23f6eb765fdb8ec986989fe1a0ebea442",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
